course: dictionary
lesson: 459
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words and sentences around them, tells you which meaning the writer wants. Armband is a good example.
explain: «Inflatable armbands and pool toys are not life-saving devices.» Inflatable means filled with air, and pool toys sit beside it, so here an armband is a small ring that children wear to help them float.
explain: «Sports teams often wear black armbands to show respect.» Teams and respect are the clues. Here an armband is a band of cloth worn around the upper arm. Check by swapping in your meaning: a blow-up ring would not show respect, so the cloth band is right.
fact: An armband can be a band of cloth worn around the upper arm to show something, such as that someone is team captain or that people are sad.
fact: An armband can also be a small inflatable ring worn on the arms to help children float while they learn to swim. Americans call these water wings or floaties.
fact: «Captain's armband» means the band that shows who leads the team.
fact: «Black armband» means a band worn to show sadness or respect.
fact: Armbands are not life jackets, so children must still be watched by an adult.
exercise: «Inflatable armbands and pool toys are not life-saving devices.» What are armbands in this sentence? | A type of life jacket | A team's score in a match | A band of cloth worn around the upper arm | *Small inflatable rings worn to help children float
exercise: «Sports teams often wear black armbands to show respect.» What does armband mean here? | A kind of life jacket | An inflatable ring for floating | A pool toy | *A band of cloth worn on the upper arm to show respect
exercise: Ella says armbands keep swimmers safe, so no adult is needed. What do the lessons say? | *Armbands are not life jackets, and children must still be watched by an adult | Armbands are life jackets, so adults can relax | Armbands only work in the sea | Armbands are only worn by team captains
test: «The captain's armband showed everyone who led the team.» What is a captain's armband? | A blow-up ring for the pool | *A cloth band worn on the arm to show who leads | A cap worn by the goalkeeper | A whistle for the referee
test: Ben, aged 13, asks if he can wear a swimming armband. He reads «If you are under 12, you must wear armbands.» What does this tell him? | Older swimmers must wear armbands by law | Only under-12s may swim at all | *The rule talks about under-12s; older swimmers may still choose them | Armbands are banned for everyone over 12
exam: Which clue in «Sports teams often wear black armbands to show respect» tells you the armband is a band of cloth, not a swimming ring? | Often means always | *Teams wear them to show respect, not to float | Black means wet | Sports means swimming
